id: throw
name: Throw
type: standard
actionCost: 1
kiCost: 0
attacking: true
requiresTarget: true
# "This is considered an Attacking Maneuver of the Simple Profile, despite its different range."
profile: simple
usageLimit: 1/round
# What is thrown is asked when it is used: an Item of the character's, or a Feature.
throws: true
source: Core Rule
description: >
  Throw something you hold: a Simple Profile attack at any range, and on a hit, Collision
  Damage as if it were a Feature. A Ki Wager of at most 1/4 of your Ki Points.
text: >
  Throw Maneuver [1/Round]: Throw an object you have on your person or in your hands.
  –Maneuver Type: Standard
  –Action Cost: 1 Action
  –KP Cost: N/A
  –Exploitable: N/A
  –Effect: You may throw whatever you are holding (such as a Basic Item, Feature, or even a
  Weapon) any number of Squares in a straight line. This is considered an Attacking Maneuver of
  the Simple Profile, despite its different range. If you hit another Character, apply
  Collision Damage as if your thrown Item was a Feature. If it was already a Feature, use the
  Hardness Rank of that Feature. If it was a Weapon, the Hardness Rank is 2. If it was a Basic
  Item, the Hardness Rank is 1.

  If you throw a Weapon, you do not apply any effects from its Qualities or its Weapon Category
  unless it possesses the Throwing Weapon Quality.

  Anything thrown at an Opponent through this Maneuver lands on a Square adjacent to them (your
  choice) if it hit, or it continues past that Opponent and lands on a Square of your ARC’s
  choosing (typically this will be at a Square that is as far as you could have possibly thrown
  it based on your Might, unless it’s stopped by a Feature first).

  You cannot Ki Wager more than 1/4 (rounded up) of your Ki Points on an Attacking Maneuver
  made through the Throw Maneuver.

---

# --- What is built -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# What is thrown is asked first: an Item the character has and is not wearing - Apparel on a
# Layer and Accessories worn are not in hand, and one in a Capsule is not on them - or a Feature,
# with its Hardness Rank. Then the attack, declared as any is, with the Simple Profile: the
# Strike against their defence, and the Wound. Not held to the Melee Range: "despite its
# different range". Its Ki Wager is capped at 1/4 of the Ki Points they have, rounded up.
#
# On a hit - the one it was thrown at, not whoever else an Area catches - Collision Damage: a
# Life Point reduction by the Hardness Value, Rank 1 for a Basic Item, 2 for a Weapon, the
# Feature's own, worked out at the base Tier of the one hit, as a Collision is. A piece whose
# Effects set its Hardness Value outright - Hefty Plating's 4 - uses that. Apparel is none of
# the three the entry names, and is read as a Basic Item, Rank 1, unless it sets its own.
#
# What an Item does thrown is its own: the Grenade gives the attack a Minor Sphere around the
# one it was thrown at and its recorded Scholarship Modifier as the Damage Attribute, and is
# gone once thrown; a piece whose Effects say `piece.thrownMightClash` - Hefty Plating - opens a
# Might Clash on a hit, won to knock them Prone.
#
# --- What the table keeps ----------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# Where it lands. The card says it lands beside the one it hit, on the thrower's choice of
# Square; missed, the ARC's. The Item stays on the character's sheet: whether it is picked up,
# and by whom, is the table's.
#
# A Weapon: Rank 2 - or the Hardness Value its Effects set, Super Heavy's 4 - and none of its
# Qualities or its Category unless it is a Throwing Weapon, whose come in only once it hits.
# Thrown from the hand it is out of hand after, but for a Boomerang taken back into it and a
# Multi-Storage Weapon's copy. A Barrage Weapon asks for the Simple or the Combination Profile.
# A Multi-Storage Weapon to throw makes this Maneuver three a Combat Round, in all.
